WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.408
Who speaks MCP.

2
00:00:01.688 --> 00:00:07.683
The protocol’s value depends on adoption, so check it against official pages rather than announcements.

3
00:00:07.963 --> 00:00:13.595
Claude Desktop connects to local stdio servers listed in a claude_desktop_config.

4
00:00:13.875 --> 00:00:18.013
json file; the MCP site’s server tutorial walks through it.

5
00:00:18.293 --> 00:00:32.011
Claude Code adds servers with claude mcp add, over HTTP (recommended for remote servers) or stdio, at three scopes: local (just you, this project), project (shared with your team through a.

6
00:00:32.291 --> 00:00:33.293
mcp.

7
00:00:33.573 --> 00:00:42.661
json file in the repository, which Claude Code asks you to approve before use in interactive sessions), and user (all your projects).

8
00:00:42.941 --> 00:00:47.293
Claude’s apps also connect to remote MCP servers as connectors.

9
00:00:47.573 --> 00:00:59.989
Outside Anthropic, OpenAI documents MCP servers for ChatGPT and for its Responses API, where an MCP tool takes an allowed-tools list and an approval setting.

10
00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:08.440
Google’s Gemini CLI reads MCP servers from its settings file and supports stdio and Streamable HTTP.

11
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.347
VS Code and Cursor configure servers in project files.

12
00:01:12.627 --> 00:01:14.867
The MCP introduction lists more.

13
00:01:15.147 --> 00:01:21.696
For model selection, this is the practical consequence: one server can serve hosts backed by different models.

14
00:01:21.976 --> 00:01:26.008
That makes MCP a fair way to compare models on your real tools.

15
00:01:26.288 --> 00:01:31.024
Connect the same server to two hosts, run the same tasks, and read the transcripts.

16
00:01:31.304 --> 00:01:38.557
Tool-use quality differs between models and versions, and the protocol guarantees only that the calls arrive well formed.

17
00:01:38.837 --> 00:01:40.715
When is MCP the wrong choice?

18
00:01:40.995 --> 00:01:51.853
If one application you own calls a tool only it needs, a plain function tool from Studio 1 is simpler: no extra process, no protocol layer, nothing to install.

19
00:01:52.133 --> 00:02:04.763
Reach for MCP when several hosts need the same capability, when you want an off-the-shelf host like Claude Code to use your internal system, or when a team should share one maintained integration.
